/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (The infection begins with a DLL sideloading technique. A legitimate executable, such as FoxitPDFReader.exe, is used to load a malicious version of msimg32.dll. To maintain the illusion of normal operation and avoid application crashes, the malicious DLL forwards standard API calls to the legitimate Windows library located in the System32 directory.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
102 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (The actual malicious payload triggers directly from the DllMain function. A multi-stage loader then decrypts and executes the core EDR killer component entirely in memory. This memory-only execution model ensures that the decrypted payload never touches the physical disk, severely limiting the artifacts available for traditional signature-based detection.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
