/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 261 0 R
/E (Halo's Gate Implementation \(Syscall Bypassing\): Security products typically place hooks inside ntdll.dll to monitor critical API calls. To bypass these, the malware utilizes a Halo's Gate technique. By scanning the ntdll.dll file forward and backward, it locates unhooked syscall stubs. It then repurposes these clean stubs to transition directly to the kernel, circumventing user-mode monitoring entirely.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
