128 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 271 0 R
/E (rwdrv.sys \(The Vulnerable Driver\): This is a renamed version of ThrottleStop.sys, a legitimate driver signed by TechPowerUp LLC \(commonly used in hardware monitoring tools like GPU-Z\). Because it has a valid digital signature, it bypasses Windows Driver Signature Enforcement. However, this driver exposes highly privileged IOCTLs that allow arbitrary read/write access to physical memory. Qilin exploits this driver to directly manipulate kernel structures, executing a classic Bring Your Own Vulnerable Driver \(BYOVD\) attack.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
